+# Scope: application decision emails
+
+**For:** VP Tech · **Module:** `modules/applications`
+
+## Goal
+
+When recruitment closes, every applicant we decided on should get exactly one
+email with our decision: an acceptance email if they were `accepted`, a
+rejection email if they were `rejected`. Today execs send these by hand, which
+is slow and has led to people getting the wrong email or none at all.
+
+## Background
+
+- Read `modules/applications/MODULE.md`, then `modules/applications/src/index.ts`.
+  The `Application` shape is in `packages/schemas/src/club.ts`.
+- Status changes go through `transition(application, to)`, which enforces the
+  pipeline. `accepted`, `rejected`, and `withdrawn` are final.
+- Applications hold personal data. The table has RLS with no policies, so only
+  the service role can read it. Everything here runs server-side.
+
+## What to build
+
+1. **Who gets what.** A pure function, e.g. `decisionEmailsDue(applications, sent)`,
+   that returns `{ application, kind: "accepted" | "rejected" }` for each final
+   decision that has not been emailed yet. Applicants still `submitted`,
+   `reviewing`, or `interview` get nothing, and `withdrawn` applicants get no
+   decision email.
+2. **Remember what was sent.** A new migration
+   `modules/applications/migrations/0002_decision_emails.sql` with a table keyed
+   by application id and kind (unique), RLS on, no policies. Insert the row in
+   the same step as sending so a re-run never sends twice.
+3. **Sending.** A server-side script the exec runs once recruitment closes.
+   It reads applications with the service role, sends via an injected
+   `sendEmail`, and prints counts (never names or emails) when done.
+4. **Docs.** Add exports to `module.json`, update `MODULE.md` and
+   `skills/run-recruitment.md` step 6, then run `pnpm catalog`.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- Writing the email copy (the President provides it) and HTML templates.
+- Interview invitations or any email before a final decision.
+- Changing statuses: this only reads them.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+- [ ] Each `accepted` applicant gets the acceptance email once; each `rejected` applicant gets the rejection email once.
+- [ ] Re-running the script after a partial failure sends only what was not sent.
+- [ ] `withdrawn` and undecided applicants get no email.
+- [ ] No applicant data appears in logs, public pages, or anything readable with the anon key.
+- [ ] `pnpm verify applications` and `pnpm check` pass.
+
+## How to verify
+
+Run `pnpm verify applications` after each change, and `pnpm check` before review.
+Test with fake applicants only; never commit real applicant data.
+
+## Open questions
+
+- Which email provider and sending address? Assumed: injected, so tests use a fake.
+- Should accepted applicants for different positions get different emails? Assumed: one template per kind, with the position filled in.
